      "summaryMarkdown": "Passed. Both findings are resolved and verified against the repair delta (bab170e..5ef0c93).\n\n- **S2-F1:** one `DeviceErrorState` per cached headless device; each headless renderer observes errors from the point it joined, and windowed error handling is unchanged.\n- **S2-F2:** the fallback for a renderer without effects now runs on every host.\n- **Port note:** the `port:` ledger convention is now described in `update-from-zed-pr.md`, in step 3 of the closure guide and in the upstream-sync memory.\n\nEverything that held in the first review still holds: windowed surface, formats and recovery; `vendor/wgpu` untouched; DX12 on Windows and Vulkan|GL on Linux; non-sRGB opaque targets with 4x path sampling; the adapter override applies only to the headless context; the static device cache is never dropped; bad target sizes return errors; Metal keeps effects false; the provenance is complete. Checks: headless_renderer 9/9 (WARP and WSL lavapipe), headless_screenshot_context 6/6.",
