    {
      "id": "S2-F1",
      "criterionIds": [
        "HEADLESS-1"
      ],
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Shared headless device routes GPU errors only to the newest renderer.**\n\n**Expected:** each renderer on the per-process cached headless device (#64842) sees the GPU errors its own work raises. Upstream does this: #64718 installs one `DeviceErrorState` per device (one lost callback, one uncaptured-error callback), and #64842 starts each new renderer at `current_generation()` because the device is shared.\n\n**Observed:** `WgpuRenderer::from_target` (`crates/gpui_wgpu/src/wgpu_renderer.rs` ~1829) calls `device.on_uncaptured_error` once for every renderer. wgpu keeps only one handler per device: `error_sink.uncaptured_handler = Some(handler)` in `vendor/wgpu/wgpu/src/backend/wgpu_core.rs:1840`. So on the device that `WgpuContext::new_headless` caches (`wgpu_context.rs:245`), only the most recently created `WgpuHeadlessRenderer` gets errors in its `last_error`. Two cases follow:\n- With two windows in one `build_with_renderer` context, window A's validation errors make window B's next render fail.\n- Once the newest renderer is dropped (a closed window or a finished test), errors from every remaining renderer go to a `last_error` that nothing reads. `render_scene_to_image` then returns `Ok` with a possibly corrupt image.\n\nThe commit body and provenance list the optional-surface adaptation but do not mention this dropped upstream behaviour.\n\n**Repair:**\n1. Install the uncaptured-error handler once per cached headless device in `create_headless`, and share it through the context the way `device_lost` is shared.\n2. Have each surface-free renderer read it with a generation counter that starts at the current generation, like Zed's `DeviceErrorState::observe_error` and `current_generation`.\n3. Skip the per-renderer `on_uncaptured_error` for surface-free renderers, so windowed behaviour stays unchanged. Extending this to windowed renderers would need a design amendment.\n4. Add a regression test, either in the `headless_renderer` group or as a `gpui_wgpu` unit test with device access. It must show that an error raised after a later renderer was created and dropped still fails the earlier renderer's next render, and that a renderer joining the device does not report errors raised before it joined.\n\n**Resolved (49e7de8):**\n- `create_headless` installs one `DeviceErrorState` per cached device (`WgpuContext::shared_errors`, `None` for windowed contexts).\n- `from_target` installs its own callback only when it has a surface, so windowed renderers are unchanged.\n- `WgpuHeadlessRenderer` starts from `current_generation()` before building its pipelines, and `check_gpu_errors` (device lost, then `observe_error`) runs before every render and after readback.\n- The new regression test covers all three cases: a later renderer created and dropped, a renderer joining after an error, and an error that reaches both renderers. It passes on WARP (9/9) and on WSL lavapipe (9/9).",
      "regressionRefs": [
        {
          "repositoryId": "gpux",
          "path": "crates/gpui_wgpu/src/wgpu_context.rs",
          "symbol": "DeviceErrorState"
        },
